{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Sorry we rolled in late. 95 was a parking lot and the garage wouldn't read my ticket, and it's like a hundred degrees out there.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Yeah the ac in this room is losing the fight. Hold on, this screen just froze again. Okay, what brings him in?",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): He's yellow. That's why. His skin.",
  "[SEG0004] person_3 (PATIENT): Mmm. Wah.",
  "[SEG0005] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sorry, yellow? Say that again, I clicked into the wrong chart.",
  "[SEG0006] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Yellow. His face and his chest, and the whites of his eyes too. And he's only feeding every four hours.",
  "[SEG0007] person_2 (DOCTOR): Every four hours. Breast or a bottle?",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Both. I nurse him and we top him off with similack, the yellow can. Umm and those vitamin d drops, d-visall, one drop a day.",
  "[SEG0009] person_2 (DOCTOR): One drop of the d-visall? Say that once more, I half heard you.",
  "[SEG0010] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Yeah. One drop, once a day. He's ten days old today.",
  "[SEG0011] person_4 (NURSE): Weight just now is 3.29 kilograms. There is a birth weight in the hospital note but that isn't today's.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): 3.29 today, thanks. When did the yellow start?",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Err I can't date it. Maybe day three, or after we got home, could've been day five or day six. I really don't know.",
  "[SEG0014] person_3 (PATIENT): Uh. Mmm mmm.",
  "[SEG0015] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. Any fever?",
  "[SEG0016] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No. No fever.",
  "[SEG0017] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any throwing up?",
  "[SEG0018] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No, he isn't vomiting.",
  "[SEG0019] person_2 (DOCTOR): How about his breathing, any trouble there?",
  "[SEG0020] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): No, breathing seems fine. He is real sleepy though. Hard to wake him to eat, the last few days.",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): Wah.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sleepy. Okay let me look while this reboots. Yeah the yellow goes down onto the chest, and the sclera are yellow. Belly's soft.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Okay. Not about him, but did you see that extra innings thing last night? I had the game on at two am and I still don't know who won.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): I missed it. I was crawling on the beltway till late, this heat has my tomatoes looking cooked on the porch.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Ha, same at our place. And they've had main street down to one lane since forever, I sat there twenty minutes just to hit the ramp. I'm just fried, sorry.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Tell me about it, I cut around by the high school. Anyway, back to him. My working thought is this is either physiologic jaundice or the breastfeeding kind, and I can't separate those without a number.",
  "[SEG0027] person_2 (DOCTOR): For the yellow, the nurse will draw a bilirubin today before you leave. No need to fast him, just before the next feed.",
  "[SEG0028] person_1 (FAMILY_MEMBER): Today, alright.",
  "[SEG0029] person_2 (DOCTOR): If that number comes back borderline we'll add a direct bilirubin, only if it's borderline. And if the yellow does not settle we'd talk about an ultrasound, I'm not ordering that now.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): I do want to see him back in two days either way. Front desk can set that.",
  "[SEG0031] person_2 (DOCTOR): And try to wake him, offer a feed every two or three hours, not stretch it to four."
 ],
